WEBVTT

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.580
Everyone! Are you fired up?!

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.370
Amazing! What a sense of unity!

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:36.830
Please enjoy yourselves to the fullest tonight.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.790
We'll be sure to sing our hearts out tonight!

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.120
Now, here's our next song!

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.290
Let's go!

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:54.790
The unending ordinary days.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:59.000
The existence known as self.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.700
Miss Yuki!

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:11.330
If suddenly, one day, without any warning,
it all disappeared...

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:15.040
Everyone! Run!

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.200
The will of those people and
their irreplaceable memories...

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:27.370
Miss Yuki!!

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:28.580
Akira!

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.660
Where would they all go?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Yuki.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.290
Souma.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.160
Come!

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:11.500
Hurry it up--

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:21.290
Hurry!

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.580
Shit!

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:19.950
"AFTERLOST"

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:25.950
"Episode 1: Lost"

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.750
I'm just a courier.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:34.160
My contract will end once I deliver you.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.370
Stay quiet until then. Got it?

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:45.830
Seriously?!

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.040
Can we make it?

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:32.410
Asshole!

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.120
Stupid bastard! What the hell are you doing?!

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.620
What in the world?!

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:07.000
What... was that just now?

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:21.700
"Horned Owl Transport"

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.330
Shit...

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:45.790
Get on!

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:48.000
Hurry!

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:53.500
"Horned Owl Transport"

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.250
They're gone?!

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:08.290
Find them! They should still be nearby!

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.410
She's within normal values for now.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.950
Hey, who the hell were those guys?!

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:23.040
I knew the Agency was dangerous,

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.660
but I was never told that
something like that would appear!

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:27.370
Check her brain waves.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.830
It seems she is still in a state of confusion.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.620
We should let her rest first.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:33.700
No need.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:37.160
I want to know what was done to her
at the facility and its effects on her.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.540
I'm the one who wants to know!

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:41.370
Explain!

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:52.910
"Three Years After Lost"
"Epic Disaster: Hundreds of
Thousands of People Missing"

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:59.410
"Natural or Man-Made Disaster?
"Crisis Control Framework in Question"

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.620
The Tama-shi.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.370
Tama-shi?

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:11.580
It seems they are victims of
the Lost three years ago.

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:15.200
So, I was attacked by a ghost?

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.040
No.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:19.450
To begin with, no one has
found a single victim's body.

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:23.410
We call them Tama-shi for
the sake of convenience.

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:29.830
And that girl, she's the lone survivor of Lost.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:31.000
Huh?

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:34.040
She's a valuable sample.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:37.950
I'm glad we were able to get her back.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:40.330
There's no need to word it that way.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:48.370
Yuki, do you remember me?

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.370
She was still pretty small at the time.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:03.290
Either way, my job here is done.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:06.080
I don't want to get involved with trouble.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.580
Make sure to transfer the funds.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:13.540
Takuya, sorry for asking you
right after you've finished a job.

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:15.830
I'd like to give you another job.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:18.910
"Lost: The City That Disappeared"
"An Area Still Shrouded in Mystery"

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.700
I want you to go to the missing city, Lost.

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:28.830
Lost? That area has been
quarantined by the government!

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:32.830
Yes. They are secretly investigating the area,

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:35.200
but there has been no
progress these last three years.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:36.330
"Analysis of Lost Impossible"
"Lack of Progress Causing
Interest of Citizens to Wane"

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:39.700
"Analysis of Lost Impossible"
"Lack of Progress Causing
Interest of Citizens to Wane"
No human has returned from there alive.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.950
Robots cannot be used there
for remote investigation.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:48.950
There are rumors that all forms of
communication within the area are blocked.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.080
To begin with, isn't that place
just a void of nothingness?

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:56.700
That's not true.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.080
The state of nothingness is there.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.830
How is that different?

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:02.830
Look at this.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:07.080
It's a message. In quantum encryption.

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.080
"YUKI I AM WAITING AT LOST"

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:12.000
"YUKI I AM WAITING AT LOST"
"Yuki, I am waiting at Lost"?

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:15.250
What's this?

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.540
This is from Yuki's father.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:24.700
My father... is alive?

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:33.290
Unfortunately, I do not know.

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:39.950
Three years ago, he tried to stop the sudden
occurrence of Lost and got caught up in it.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:43.790
After all this time,
we received a message from him.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:50.120
Either way, if you go to Lost,
you may be able to discover some clues.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:57.080
So, the thing you want me to deliver...

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:59.330
Yes. Yuki.

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:02.000
I want you to deliver Yuki to Lost.

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:07.870
Takuya, you are the only person I can ask.

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:10.700
"YUKI I AM WAITING AT LOST"

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:17.330
The pay better be good.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:23.000
Of course.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:43.120
"Yua-tan" "I Love Yua"

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:47.700
"Yua-tan" "I Love Yua"
I wonder where I should have
my loner RL meeting this year?

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.790
"Yua-tan" "I Love Yua"

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.540
Hey, Geek.

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:55.830
Takuya!

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:58.330
Geez, don't scare me like that!

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:00.580
You're handsome even when you're angry.

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:02.160
Shut up.

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.080
Can you take a look at her?

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:05.830
Sure, I guess.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.040
Who is that girl?

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:15.660
No way, Takuya! You finally
resorted to kidnapping?!

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:18.000
Well, something like that.

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:22.120
I should be able to fix her up
in about 30 minutes...

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:24.660
You can munch on that while you wait.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:28.870
Uh, no thanks.

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:33.870
So, where are you going with such a cutie?

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.950
A date? I won't forgive you.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:41.700
Oh, some things happened.
And now I'm heading to Lost.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.410
Takuya! Come here a sec!

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.410
Are you crazy?!

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:54.160
Huh? That girl?

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:57.370
She's the lone survivor of Lost?

00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:00.250
Seems like it.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:05.910
I know you're not the type to get
blinded by some money, Takuya.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.700
But this is way too dangerous.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:11.410
Look, you're already injured as it is.

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:13.040
Part of the job.

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:14.750
Even so, something like this...

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:16.950
I follow through on my contracts.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:19.750
It's my personal policy.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:23.870
No matter what it is,
I deliver what I'm hired to deliver.

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.080
I know.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.370
But you're walking straight into your own grave!

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.660
Is there a need to go so far for that girl?

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:34.580
Isn't she a stranger?

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:40.910
Stranger or not, she's just a package.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:51.330
Shit.

00:14:04.950 --> 00:14:07.620
Father... Souma...

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:14.500
Akira...

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.000
It has been three years.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:21.910
Various prefectures are doing demonstrations
in honor of the victims of Lost.

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:25.290
The government should announce
the truth to the public!

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:28.040
Announce the truth! Announce the truth!

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.910
I can see it.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:36.700
The alignment of your stars...

00:14:36.700 --> 00:14:39.790
The fate upon your shoulders is a heavy one.

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:54.120
Takuya, it seems the Agency has
expanded their search to this area.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.660
To ensure our own safety, we are on the move.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:59.750
Find a route to Lost and head
that way as soon as possible.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:03.500
I'd love to do that, but the girl is gone.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:06.580
What?!

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:12.660
Where did she go?

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:14.700
Did I say something I shouldn't have?!

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.750
An acquaintance of mine is looking for her.

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:19.200
I will head to Lost as soon as I find her.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.700
"Incoming call"
"Takuya"

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:34.790
Hey.

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:37.120
It's been a while, Takuya.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:40.500
Sorry for the sudden call, but I need
you to check something out for me.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.000
What is it?

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.500
Tell me a route to enter Lost.

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:48.620
You're heading to Lost?
What in the world are you...

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:50.410
Please just tell me!

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:55.620
I understand.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:59.330
I have some data from a previous search.
I'll send it over to you.

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.660
Thanks. I'm depending on you.

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:07.410
He really hasn't changed at all.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:22.250
Turn back now.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:25.450
Otherwise, you will...

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:31.910
There is no place for me to go back...

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:40.040
What do you plan on doing alone? Get on.

00:16:41.410 --> 00:16:43.290
Hurry up and get on.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.830
You're going, right?

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.540
To your father?

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:55.000
It's fine if you don't believe in me.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:58.200
But you saw that message.

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:02.040
At the very least, believe in your father.

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:35.370
Looks like you're really precious to them.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.950
It's fine.

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.870
We'll just lose them again.

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:50.330
Seriously?!

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.120
Shit!

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:39.450
Enough!

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:43.160
There's no meaning!
You have nothing to do with this!

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:45.580
Even if I go to Lost...!

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:51.620
...they're all dead! Even my father!

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:53.580
Don't give up.

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:56.500
Did you confirm that with your own eyes?

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:58.620
You won't know unless you go!

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:03.830
It all disappeared. Everything!

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:06.830
Confirm it. With your own eyes.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.080
At this rate, even you...

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:25.870
Akira?!

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:31.790
Did you call him here?

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:45.620
Yuki!

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.250
We should be out of their range...

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:29.330
I apologize for causing you trouble.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:31.750
Make sure to collect her properly.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:36.000
You can kill the guy.

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.450
Yes.

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:39.120
Oh, that's right.

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:44.330
Suzuna. Why didn't you
report the situation sooner?

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:49.750
Did you think you could get ahead of me?

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:03.750
Was this really the best course of action?

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:06.160
What do you mean?

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:06.700
"Three Years After Lost" "Epic Disaster:
Hundreds of Thousands of People Missing"

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:11.160
"Three Years After Lost" "Epic Disaster:
Hundreds of Thousands of People Missing"
You know very well the
dangers of approaching Lost.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:16.160
To begin with, there hasn't been
a single person who has reached it...

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:23.450
At the very least, the Agency will
not kill her while she still has value.

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:25.120
But, what about him?

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:29.450
Either way, he will be a valuable sample.

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:32.870
The Observer will decide the rest.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:54.120
He is still breathing.

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:55.910
I will do it.

00:23:43.250 --> 00:23:44.000
"Sacrifice"

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:46.200
"Sacrifice"
Next episode: "Sacrifice."

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:46.950
"Sacrifice"
